The forward lens's count (line 7 of 1.0) refers to schema 1.0's count through
the lineage rather than to v0_0, found by checkReferences at bind. A lens may
refer only to the instance it takes, its own body and CUE's builtin packages.

The position is the referring field of v1_0, looked up in the lens value by
the finding's path, so the error lands on the author's line. The reference
itself is read from the lens's syntax, which has no positions.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count?: int
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count: int & <10
}

forward: {
	count: to.schema.count
}

backward: {
	count: to.count
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
schema: {
	title: string
	count: int & <10
}

forward: {
	count: to.schema.count
}

backward: {
	count: to.count
}
-- out/error --
v1_0.count in lens 0.0->1.0 refers to schemas["1"]["0"].schema.count, a schema:
    ship/history/1.0.thema:7:9
-- out/positions --
v1_0.count in lens 0.0->1.0 refers to schemas["1"]["0"].schema.count, a schema
	authored ship/history/1.0.thema:7:9
